  "id": "Kingston-26_00007_FUL",
  "appeal_status": null,
  "appeal_start_date": null,
  "description": "The proposal is for a community facility under F1 use class which offers a learning and multipurpose hall for the local community from the vacant premises formerly used as aDental Surgery which has moved.",
  "development_type": "Other change of use",
  "decision_conditions": [
    "The development hereby permitted shall begin before the expiration of three years from the date of this permission.\r\rReason: This is required by Section 91 of the Town and Country Planning Act 1990 (as amended).",
    "Prior to the commencement of any development above ground level, details of waste and recycling facilities to serve the development to which this permission relates shall be submitted to and approved in writing by the local planning authority. \r\rThe refuse and recycling facilities as shown in the approved details shall be provided prior to beneficial occupation of the development and shall be permanently retained thereafter. The developer and/or their successors in title shall take all reasonable steps to ensure that all refuse and recyclable materials associated with the development are either stored within these facilities or internally within the building(s) on the application site, and that no refuse or recycling material is stored or placed for collection on the public highway except on the day of collection.\r\rReason: To ensure proper waste management in the interests of the character and appearance of the area and the living conditions of neighbouring occupiers, in accordance with policy SI 7 of the London Plan 2021 and policies CS9 and DM10 of the LDF Core Strategy 2012.",
    "Prior to the commencement of any development above ground level, details of secure cycle parking facilities to serve the development to which this permission relates shall be submitted to and approved in writing by the local planning authority.\r\rThe cycle parking facilities as shown in the approved details shall be provided prior to beneficial occupation of the development to which this permission relates and shall be permanently retained for that purpose and kept free from obstruction thereafter.\r\rReason: To ensure that appropriate opportunities to promote sustainable transport are taken up, in accordance with policy T5 of the London Plan 2021 and policies CS6 and DM8 of the LDF Core Strategy 2012.",
    "The site and building works required to implement the development shall be only carried out between the hours of 08.00 and 18.00 Mondays to Fridays and between 08.00 and 13.00 on Saturdays and not at all on Bank Holidays and Sundays\r\rReason: To safeguard the amenity of the neighbours by minimising impacts of the development that would otherwise give rise to nuisance.",
    "The use of the development hereby permitted shall operate only between the hours of 07:00 and 21:00 each day.  \r\rReason: To safeguard the amenity of the neighbours by minimising impacts of the development that would otherwise give rise to nuisance.",
    "Prior to the beneficial occupation of the development hereby permitted, a scheme of sound insulation and acoustic ventilation shall be implemented in full and permanently retained thereafter to ensure that internal noise levels do not exceed 35 dBLAeq, 16 hour in living rooms and bedrooms during the daytime (0700 to 2300 hours), and 30 dBLAeq, 8 hour and 45 dBLAFmax in bedrooms during the night time (2300 to 0700 hours) in accordance with BS8233:2014. Where these levels cannot be met with windows open, the scheme shall include appropriate acoustic ventilation, such as a passive vent, variable speed mechanical air supply unit, or whole house ventilation, which provides sufficient ventilation without compromising the specified noise level standards.\r\rReason: To ensure satisfactory living conditions for future occupants of the development and neighbouring occupiers, in accordance with Policy D14 of the London Plan (2021) and Policy DM10 of the Kingston Core Strategy (2012)"
  ],
